From: Shiras Rahman U <shirasra@qti.qualcomm.com>
Date: Mon, 12 May 2026 09:07:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] This patch addresses compilation warnings and errors in the WAN Manager component by fixing type mismatches, correcting printf/scanf format specifiers, resolving improper function pointer casts, and improving string handling safety through buffer size increases and use of safer APIs like strlcpy and strtok_r. It also includes platform-specific functional fixes such as updating the default WAN interface to eth0, correcting the CLIENT_DUID_FILE path, adding MTU-aware gateway route configuration, and triggering dhcp_server-restart for Cellular interfaces during IPv4 setup.

Signed-off-by: Shiras Rahman U <shirasra@qti.qualcomm.com>

